 "result_text": "`create_pull_request` in `git_machete/github.py` now sends the POST straight away. It no longer calls `derive_pull_requests` first to check whether a PR already exists. I didn't run any tests, and I couldn't lint because `flake8` isn't installed here.\n\nIf a PR for that branch already exists, GitHub answers with a 422. `client.py` already catches that as `UnprocessableEntityHTTPError`, using the error text from the response body.\n\nThe old message included the existing PR's link and details, and the 422 text may not. I didn't check what GitHub puts in that body for an existing PR. I also didn't look at what `client.py` does with the error.\n\nI also removed the `find_or_none` import from `github.py`, since nothing else in that file used it.",
